# Tracer: compile a definition-resolved builtin computation without target-side search.
#
# Before:
# have one Z = 1
# have integer_set set = Z
# one + 1 $in integer_set
#
# Former behavior: Litex could not verify the final source fact, so no Lean IR existed.
#
# Now:
have one Z = 1
have integer_set set = Z

one + 1 $in integer_set

# Current behavior: Lean replays the closed `2 $in Z` computation, normalizes
# it to `1 + 1 $in Z`, and applies the exact stored definition equalities for
# `one` and `integer_set`.
#
# Boundary: `have unknown_set set` supplies no definition equality, so
# `one + 1 $in unknown_set` remains rejected before Lean emission.
